            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to give away, then the Persian for guilty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: محکوم شدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محکوم شدن (mahkum shodan) — \"to be sentenced, to be convicted\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مرد به دو سال زندان محکوم شد. Mard be do sâl zendân mahkum shod. The man was sentenced to two years in prison."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The punishment takes be. Present mahkum mishavad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mahkum is usually traced to Arabic maḥkūm, \"judged, ruled on\"; EtymDB lists no entry. shodan \"to become\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
