          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زندانی (zendâni) — \"a prisoner\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زندانی (zendâni) ها هر روز یک ساعت در حیاط بودند. Zendâni-hâ har ruz yek sâ'at dar hayât budand. The prisoners spent an hour in the yard every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zendân \"prison\" + -i. Also an adjective, \"imprisoned\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zendâni adds the suffix -i to zendân \"prison\", a native Persian word; EtymDB links zendân to Old Armenian zndan but gives it no parent, so its deeper origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
